<title>SOUTH KOREA: Ssangyong Oil final '96 net up slightly.</title>
<headline>Ssangyong Oil final '96 net up slightly.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-03-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>	  (in billion won unless stated)</p>
<p>    Share (won)				2,197    vs 2,114</p>
<p>    Net profit				   124.34 vs   119.70</p>
<p>Dividend (pct, cash, per 5,000 won)</p>
<p>	common shares			     26.0  vs    30.0</p>
<p>	preferred shares			  27.0  vs    31.0</p>
<p>    Turnover				   4,461.24 vs 3,474.31</p>
<p>    Pre-tax profit			     157.18 vs   174.21</p>
<p>    Extraordinaries		     6.87 (gain) vs 0.65 (loss)</p>
<p>NOTE - Ssangyong Oil Refining Co is a unit of the Ssangyong at the end of 1996, unchanged from a year earlier. An official at the company said last month its net profit was expected to reach about 120 billion won.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727-5646</p>
</text>
